# ADR-016: File Storage Strategy

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| ADR | 016 |
| Title | File Storage Strategy |
| Status | Accepted |
| Date | 2026-07-27 |
| Decision Makers | R-zension Engineering Team |

---

# Context

R-zension will manage various types of user-generated and system-generated files throughout its lifecycle.

Examples include

- User profile images
- Organization logos
- Documents
- AI-generated reports
- Exported analytics
- Attachments
- Future media assets

Storing binary files directly in the relational database would negatively impact database performance, increase backup size, and reduce scalability.

A dedicated storage strategy is required.

---

# Decision

R-zension will separate **metadata storage** from **binary file storage**.

- PostgreSQL stores file metadata.
- Binary files are stored in dedicated object storage.
- The application references files using unique identifiers and URLs.

---

# Storage Architecture

```text
User

↓

Frontend

↓

Express Backend

↓

Validation

↓

Object Storage

↓

File Metadata

↓

PostgreSQL
```

---

# Objectives

The storage system should

- Scale independently
- Support large files
- Improve database performance
- Secure uploaded content
- Enable future CDN integration
- Simplify backups

---

# Storage Responsibilities

## PostgreSQL

Stores

- File ID
- Owner
- Organization
- File name
- MIME type
- Size
- Storage path
- Upload date
- Version
- Status

Never stores

- Binary content

---

## Object Storage

Stores

- Images
- Documents
- Reports
- Attachments
- Export files
- AI-generated assets

